# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings on every platform.
#
# The coordination subsystem's source guards read the crate's own source as
# text and cut each file at literal `\n#[cfg(test)]\n` markers. A checkout
# that converts to CRLF (Git for Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`)
# hides those markers, so test modules are scanned as production and
# twenty-eight guards fail at once — measured on the first native Windows run
# of the suite. The shell scripts under `scripts/` need LF as well.
#
# Git detects binary content itself; `text=auto` leaves it alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
